This is a fun turn-based strategy game with a decent plot (notting awesome here). If you are not used to the genre, think of this as a more elaborate chess game. I didn't play it on multiplayer mode, so I can't review that part of the experience.
I had a good time in my playtroght, but I think I should point out some issues:
-the camera sometimes can be problematic specially when you are trying to move form one floor to another;
-the game gets quite repetitive after you played for some time;
-the story moves really fast, so unless you delay it, you wont be able to explore all items and types of missions you could otherwise;
But the really sad thing about this game it does not give you many options in any sort of way: you have 4 classes of soldiers each one with its own tech tree (even though some classes mix up a bit), but this tech trees are basicly limited to only 2 different options per level. Besides that, you dont get more than 2 options of weapons for each class. So you end up with a feeling that this game could have so much more in it. More weapons, more skills, more costumization, more...
Besides all this, the game is still really fun, and I think you should play it. Having a lot of variety is not a must, but it would make this good game be an awsome one.

