Batman Arkham Knight is the last game of the series that is set nine months after Arkham City finishes. Where you are noq in Gotham the home of Batman and the underground criminals we all know. suddenly thrown against two protagonist Scarecrow; who wants to crush Gotham into a city of Fear, and the mysterious Arkham Knight; who despises you Batman.
The game picks up from the amazing gadgets and gives you further tools to thawt their attack on Gotham.
The narrative its very good and compelling for me to play; the batmobile yes; the combat of the batmobile is sadly not;
while its battle tank mode is able to switch on the fly; is a simple to grasp combat; with side swiping to avoid visual cues of enemy fire direction. The repeatative nature of using the batmobile in the side quests would likely be tedious (I have not gone into many SQ yet but the Main Narrative.)
The game has emphasis on the bat mobile on puzzles which i find very awesome compared to others who finds it annoying. The Batmobile ambushes for one are amazing moments that i found it memorable where you are trapped with men waiting for you and sentry guna trained on the doorway waiting for your appearance; to what looka like you cant get out; then you remember the remote control of batmobile. You enter the parking lot; go straight to the roof...
And gun them all down with non lethal weapons for men and take down the two sentry's with 60mm fire.
